! AlAs: the Berry-phase polarization along the third reciprocal lattice vector.
!
! The ground state is `alas-raman.in`'s -- the same cell, cutoff, k-grid and
! `nosym`/`noinv` -- so the two cases share a converged density and this input
! is only the `lberry` post-processing on top of it.
!
! Two things about the settings are deliberate and both are recorded in
! `reference.out.alas-berry` beside this file:
!
!   * `conv_thr = 1e-12`, where the pw_berry test-suite cases leave it at the
!     default. At the default the two symmetry-equivalent strings of this k-set
!     come out 1e-5 apart (0.00250 against 0.00251) and the electronic phase is
!     0.00875; tightened, they agree with each other exactly and the phase is
!     0.00876. The looser number is not the converged one.
!   * `nppstr = 6` counts the repeated endpoint, as `kp_strings` lays it out --
!     six points spanning the whole reciprocal vector, the last being the
!     first one's periodic image. The string carries five *distinct* points.
!
! AlAs is zincblende and non-centrosymmetric, so its total phase is not pinned
! to 0 or half a quantum by symmetry the way a diamond crystal's is.
 &control
    calculation = 'nscf'
    lberry = .true.
    gdir = 3
    nppstr = 6
    prefix = 'alas'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.575, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 10.0
    nosym = .true.
    noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-12
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98  Al.pz-vbc.UPF
 As  74.92  As.pz-bhs.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Al 0.00 0.00 0.00
 As 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 2 2 6 0 0 0
